           OUTER EXTENT, as a length any box that must contain the ring can reserve.
           `outline-offset` seats the ring OUTSIDE the control box, so the paint reaches
           offset + width beyond it — 4px at the house geometry. That is a fact about the
           ring, derived from the two terms directly above rather than restated as a
           literal, so a retune of either moves the reservation with it. `run.css` is its
           one consumer today (the scroll port is the box that was cutting the ring off);
           it lives HERE, with the terms it is computed from, because a reserve that
           drifts from the ring it reserves for is worse than none. */
        --dock-ring-reserve: calc(var(--dock-ring-width) + var(--dock-ring-offset));
    }

