       the reason is a collision rather than a preference.

       ~~`box-shadow: var(--dock-ring); outline: none;`~~ — `box-shadow` is ONE property
       and the dock was asking it to carry two independent facts: this focus ring, and
       every control's own hover/press/selected elevation. A single property cannot hold
       two states, so whichever rule wins the cascade ERASES the other — which is why the
       comment above has to explain that the group deliberately keeps class specificity
       "NOT `:where()`, which would … let a per-control :hover box-shadow override the
       focus ring". That paragraph is the defect describing its own workaround: the
       specificity ladder exists to stop a hover from deleting a keyboard user's focus
       ring, and it only holds until the next control ships a more specific hover.

       `outline` is a DIFFERENT property. It composes with any elevation instead of
       competing with it, it is what forced-colors mode actually honours (a `box-shadow`
       ring vanishes entirely under a forced-colors palette — a total loss of focus
       visibility, not a degraded one), and `outline-offset` seats it OUTSIDE the control
       box so it never overlaps the glyph it surrounds. The old `outline: none` was
       therefore not a tidy-up beside the shadow: it was the line that removed the only
       channel a high-contrast user had.

       THE REGISTER SURVIVES, RE-EXPRESSED. `--dock-ring` was a whole `box-shadow` LIST,
       which is the only shape a shadow ring can take; an outline takes three separate
       terms, so the one register becomes the `--dock-ring-{width,offset,color}` trio
       declared above. A consumer still retunes every dock ring from one place and now
       retunes each term independently instead of re-authoring a two-stop shadow string.
       `--dock-ring` itself (`src/styles/tokens/sizing.css:255`) is left standing: it is
       outside Lane α's fence and `dark-mode-toggle.css:31` still reads it as a fallback.
       Its orphaning-or-retarget rides the marked addendum with the rest of W8's
       tokens-file half. */
    .dock-icon-button:focus-visible,
    .dock-tab-button:focus-visible,
    .dock-select-trigger:focus-visible,
    .dock-dropdown-trigger:focus-visible {
        outline: var(--dock-ring-width) solid var(--dock-ring-color);
        outline-offset: var(--dock-ring-offset);
    }

    /* The ACTIVE SEAT yields to consumer indicator content — a control hosting the
       consumer's own indicator suppresses the dock ring so that content reads.
       [2026-08-24 · BK #47 W8 MATERIAL] Re-pointed with the ring: ~~`box-shadow:
       none`~~ suppressed a ring that no longer rides `box-shadow`, so it would have
       yielded nothing while still deleting whatever elevation the control carried. A
       yield must name the property the ring is actually on. */
    .glass-dock [data-ring-yield]:focus-visible {
        outline: none;
    }

    .dock-icon-button:disabled,
    .dock-tab-button:disabled,
    .dock-select-trigger:disabled,
    .dock-dropdown-trigger:disabled,
    .dock-icon-button[aria-disabled="true"],
    .dock-tab-button[aria-disabled="true"] {
        opacity: var(--opacity-disabled);
        cursor: not-allowed;
    }
}

